Did I ever tell you about the time I found Henry Kissinger's shapewear in an abandoned storage unit? What a trip, let me tell you. We were somewhere near the Virginia State line in the Blue Ridge mountains, close enough to see decommissioned radio telescopes in the National Radio Quiet Zone. 
I was in the area and got it in my head to check in with my friend Remir. Remir and I met on an icebreaker in the North Pacific. After that thing with the ratcatchers in Alberta, Johnny had gotten us passage back into the states in exchange for overnight engineer shifts. Remir's parents were soviet expats who didn't appreciate the westernization of Russia after the Iron Curtain came down, they wanted more privacy. We spent most of our time rescuing rich kids who needed to learn a lesson before they could join their parents in whatever c-suite they were destined for. But I'm getting distracted. Remir's parents had left him a storage facility that hadn't been touched in years after a hillariously corrupt lawyer "lost" the probate documents during her arrest for forging baseball cards. 
On paper the facility was a self-storage facility in climate-controlled barn. In reality, it was a labyrinth of private offices that obscenely powerful people used to hide their "passion projects". It wasn't that, get your mind out of the gutter. Plenty of CEOs and more than a few Cabinet Secretaries preferred to unwind with a bottle of Scotch old enough to rent a car and oil paints. 
No one had touched any of the storage units in at least ten years, our entire mission today was to make sure our keys worked and the doors were still sealed. Because the average client lease was measured in decades, the facility had equally long-termed contracts with maintenence and janitorial services, and the main barn at least had been operational the entire time. When the door opened, the air coming out of the barn smelled like a freshly cleaned hospital room, with a faint smell of industrial strength cleaner in the purified air. Remir said a short prayer in Russian and we went inside. 
